  "id": "COMPOUND:16888 - PROTEIN:2575",
  "verbalization": "Theasaponin E1 is implicated in the regulation of Cyclin-dependent kinase 7 (CDK7) through a series of molecular interactions involving 4-(3-Pyridin-2-Yl-1h-Pyrazol-4-Yl)Quinoline. This compound acts as a target of multiple kinases, including Tyrosine-protein kinase Blk, Phosphatidylinositol 4-phosphate 3-kinase C2 domain-containing subunit beta, and Serine/threonine-protein kinase 33. These kinases are themselves targets of the same quinoline compound, which in turn directly targets CDK7. The consistent presence of this quinoline compound as a common mediator across different target pathways suggests a central role in the signaling network that leads to CDK7 activation. The evidence supports a mechanism where Theasaponin E1 indirectly influences CDK7 through the activation of these intermediate kinases, highlighting a potential regulatory pathway that involves the quinoline compound as a key mediator.",
